{"abstract":"In this paper, we use spectral analysis to investigate transfer learning and study model sensitivity to frequency shortcuts in medical imaging. By analyzing the power spectrum density of both pre-trained and fine-tuned model gradients, as well as artificially generated frequency shortcuts, we observe notable differences in learning priorities between models pre-trained on natural vs medical images, which generally persist during fine-tuning. We find that when a model's learning priority aligns with the power spectrum density of an artifact, it results in overfitting to that artifact. Based on these observations, we show that source data editing can alter the model's resistance to shortcut learning. ...","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lu, Yucheng","Juodelyte, Dovile","Victor, Jonathan D.","Cheplygina, Veronika"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776460"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cornell University"],"keyword":["Medical imaging","Shortcut Learning","Transfer learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring connections of spectral analysis and transfer learning in medical imaging","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2407.11379","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776460","ids":["itu-f77bf527-2516-4407-8793-12b89de999f9"],"keyword":["Image statistics","Medical imaging","Shortcut learning","Transfer learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-E831ED914F9C98160593D2160ECFECFC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2407.11379","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Data-intensive Systems and Applications","IT University of Copenhagen, Data, Systems, and Robotics, Pattern Recognition Revisited lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"cornell university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cornell University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yucheng","key":"lupau","last":"Lu","locid":"864e737f-8deb-4b43-8403-8edb558e8567","name":"Lu, Yucheng","orcid":"0000-0003-2990-5252","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dovile","key":"juodelytepau","last":"Juodelyte","locid":"6800c64b-0e54-49cb-a703-384b4987b70c","name":"Juodelyte, Dovile","orcid":"0000-0002-6195-1120","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonathan D.","key":"victorpau","last":"Victor","name":"Victor, Jonathan D.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Veronika","key":"cheplyginapau","last":"Cheplygina","locid":"1c4bfd79-4336-4b17-a672-9acb465f15c0","name":"Cheplygina, Veronika","orcid":"0000-0003-0176-9324","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2407.11379","pages":"11","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f77bf527-2516-4407-8793-12b89de999f9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exploring connections of spectral analysis and transfer learning in medical imaging ...","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776460","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Broomcorn millet (Panicum miliaceum) is among the earliest domesticated staple crops in the world’s agricultural history and facilitated the development of several early agrarian cultures, particularly those originating in northern China. However, the propagation route of broomcorn millet in China from the Middle Ages to the present remains unclear. The aim of this study is to explore the genetic affinity between ancient and modern millet samples, trace the genetic origins and diffusion pathways of broomcorn millet, and provide insights into its domestication and spread. To achieve this, we sequence ancient DNA from broomcorn millet remains excavated from the Chashan Village cemetery (AD 691) in Gansu Province, China. Phylogenetic and population genetic analyses, integrating ancient and modern millet genomes, reveal a close genetic relationship between ancient millet and contemporary millet from Ningxia Province (445 km away from Chashan Village), suggesting a potential origin for the Chashan millet. This finding aligns with the tomb’s epitaph, which documents the reburial of the tomb’s owner, who was originally buried in Ningxia, and provides important archaeological evidence for understanding the interaction between geopolitical dynamics and the natural environment in northwest China during the late seventh century. Furthermore, outgroup-f3 and D statistics evidence suggests substantial genetic interactions between ancient millet and modern varieties from the Loess Plateau, Huang-Huai-Hai Plain, and Northeast Plain, indicating the dispersal route of broomcorn millet, along with human migration routes, from the northwest to northern China and ultimately to the northeast region, starting from the Middle Ages onward. This study enhances our understanding of millet’s genetic history, offers a novel perspective on burial archaeology, and provides valuable insights into the origins, domestication, and diffusion of broomcorn millet.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Sun, Xiaolan","Wang, Yifan","Lu, Yongxiu","Xu, Yongxiang","Liu, Bingbing","Yang, Yishi","Chen, Guoke","Wang, Hongru","Huang, Zihao","Cai, Yuanyang","Gu, Zhengquan","Wang, Xiaoxia","Dong, Guanghui","Wang, Yucheng"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-764658"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["China","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Agricultural Sciences","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Gansu Provincial Institute of Cultural Relics and Archaeology","Lanzhou University","University of Cambridge"],"keyword":["Ancient DNA","Broomcorn millet","Genetic diversity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ancient genome of broomcorn millet from northwest china in seventh century ce shedding new light to its origin and dispersal patterns","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/agronomy14092004","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-764658","identifier":[{"id":"85205037899","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-156087f5-df4e-4b02-8afe-ae97eeb71343"],"keyword":["ancient DNA","broomcorn millet","genetic diversity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6A0807D37B8844900144B4CBF8D1B34E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/agronomy14092004","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/409231500/agronomy_14_02004_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"lanzhou university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Lanzhou University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"gansu provincial institute of cultural relics and archaeology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Gansu Provincial Institute of Cultural Relics and Archaeology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of agricultural sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Agricultural Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"university of cambridge","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cambridge","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Globe Institute, Section for Geogenetics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Xiaolan","key":"sunxiaolanpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Xiaolan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yifan","key":"wangyifanpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Yifan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yongxiu","key":"luyongxiupau","last":"Lu","name":"Lu, Yongxiu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yongxiang","key":"xuyongxiangpau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Yongxiang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Bingbing","key":"liubingbingpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Bingbing","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Yishi","key":"yangyishipau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Yishi","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Guoke","key":"chenguokepau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Guoke","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Hongru","key":"wanghongrupau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Hongru","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","first":"Zihao","key":"huangzihaopau","last":"Huang","name":"Huang, Zihao","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Yuanyang","key":"caiyuanyangpau","last":"Cai","name":"Cai, Yuanyang","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Zhengquan","key":"guzhengquanpau","last":"Gu","name":"Gu, Zhengquan","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xiaoxia","key":"wangxiaoxiapau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Xiaoxia","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Guanghui","key":"dongguanghuipau","last":"Dong","name":"Dong, Guanghui","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5 6","first":"Yucheng","key":"wangyuchengpau","last":"Wang","locid":"176fcd28-3367-4699-9c07-3ce481df6cb3","name":"Wang, Yucheng","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/agronomy14092004","issn":["20734395"],"issue":"9","journal":"Agronomy","paperid":"2004","status":"p","title":"Agronomy","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85205037899"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-156087f5-df4e-4b02-8afe-ae97eeb71343"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Ancient Genome of Broomcorn Millet from Northwest China in Seventh Century CE : Shedding New Light to Its Origin and Dispersal Patterns","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-764658","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Halide perovskites are enticing candidates for highly efficient planar light-emitting diodes (LEDs) with commercial potential in displays and lighting. However, it remains a challenge for conventional solution fabrication processes to fabricate large-scale or non-planar LEDs due to the non-uniformity of perovskite films in conjunction with material stability issues. Here large-area highly uniform arrays of crystalline perovskite quantum wires are grown with emission spectra covering the whole visible range. Photoluminescence quantum yield of up to 92% and 5,644 hours as the time for photoluminescence to degrade down to its 50% of the initial value under ambient conditions are achieved for MAPbBr3 quantum wires. LEDs based on these quantum wires on rigid and flexible planar substrates are fabricated up to a four-inch wafer size and also unique three-dimensional spherical LEDs with outstanding uniformity are reported. The results suggest that the approach developed here can be generalized to other unconventional three-dimensional LEDs in the future.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Zhang, Daquan","Zhang, Qianpeng","Ren, Beitao","Zhu, Yudong","Abdellah, Mohamed","Fu, Yu","Cao, Bryan","Wang, Chen","Gu, Leilei","Ding, Yucheng","Tsui, Kwong-Hoi","Fan, Sufeng","Poddar, Swapnadeep","Shu, Lei","Zhang, Yuting","Kuang, Dai-Bin","Liao, Jin-Feng","Lu, Yang","Zheng, Kaibo","He, Zhubing","Fan, Zhiyong"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-305126"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Fan, Zhiyong"],"country":["China","Hong Kong","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","City University of Hong Kong","Hong Kong University of Science and Technology","Lund University","Southern University of Science and Technology","Sun Yat-Sen University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"large scale planar and spherical light emitting diodes based on arrays of perovskite quantum wires","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85127383083","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-305126","identifier":[{"id":"85127383083","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-01ed6523-8561-44b9-8698-59db7771147b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-5F1F1299D029CE42CD0450B8B4955627"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"hk","key":"hong kong university of science and technology","loc":["Hong Kong","Asia, East"],"name":"Hong Kong University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"hk","key":"city university of hong kong","loc":["Hong Kong","Asia, East"],"name":"City University of Hong Kong","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"sun yat sen university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sun Yat-Sen University","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"cn","key":"southern university of science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Southern University of Science and Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daquan"